  "title": "Collinear Triples and Cubic Curves",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Fix $k$. Let $A \\subset \\mathbb{R}^2$ be a set of $n$ points with no more than $k$ on any line. Suppose at least $\\delta n^2$ pairs $(x, y) \\in A \\times A$ have the line $xy$ containing a third point of $A$. Is there a cubic curve containing at least $cn$ points of $A$?",
